# Trivy CVE exceptions for orkyo-community
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # Impact | Reason | Added: YYYY-MM-DD | Review: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Policy: time-bound only. Review date must be within 14 days of added date.
# Remove entries once the upstream fix is available.

# ── Trivy false positive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy reports fix as 12.6.5 but KC ships mssql-jdbc 13.2.1.jre11 (newer); false positive.
CVE-2025-59250  # HIGH | mssql-jdbc: improper input validation — Trivy compares the installed 13.2.1 against a fix list ending 13.2.1.jre11 and calls it older; the shipped JAR is the fixed version, false positive (re-verified 2026-09-12 on quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.7.3) | Added: 2026-09-12 | Review: 2026-09-26

# ── Keycloak base OS layer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2026-09-03: the KC-26.6.x-era entries that stood in this file (jackson-databind,
# micrometer, OpenJDK, libacl, pgjdbc, six netty, a jackson-core GHSA, and the two sqlite
# FTS5 ones) are gone from the image this repo actually ships — the nightly security refresh
# rebuilt the foundation KC base out from under them. Verified against the artifact CI scans,
# ghcr.io/kymr10n/orkyo-community-keycloak:sha-b1290a37, both with CI's flags and with
# --ignore-unfixed OFF: the only findings are the mssql-jdbc false positive above and the
# entry below.

# ── Alpine util-linux 2.42.1-r0 — nginx-alpine runtime (frontend) ─────────────
# 2026-09-12: seven HIGH findings reported against libuuid, which Alpine builds from
# the util-linux source package. Every one of them is in util-linux's own mount(8)
# or nsenter(1) — local privilege escalation through TOCTOU races, nosuid/noexec
# bypass, privileged X-mount post-hooks and cgroup authority leaks.
#
# Neither program is in this image. Verified 2026-09-12 inside the pinned digest:
# the util-linux package is not installed, libuuid ships exactly two files
# (usr/lib/libuuid.so.1 and libuuid.so.1.3.0, UUID generation only), and /bin/mount,
# /bin/umount and /usr/bin/nsenter all resolve to /bin/busybox. Trivy attaches the
# CVEs at source-package level, so libuuid inherits them from code it does not carry.
# The container also runs as a non-root user.
#
# Same finding and same reasoning as orkyo-saas, which shares this base image.
# `apk upgrade` is not an option — see CLAUDE.md. Clears itself when upstream
# rebuilds: nightly security-refresh.yml picks the new package up.
CVE-2026-53612  # HIGH | util-linux mount(8) TOCTOU (libuuid 2.42.1-r0, fix 2.42.3-r0) | mount(8) is busybox here; util-linux package not installed | Added: 2026-09-12 | Review: 2026-09-26
CVE-2026-53613  # HIGH | util-linux mount(8) TOCTOU via ancestor directory swap (libuuid 2.42.1-r0, fix 2.42.3-r0) | mount(8) is busybox here; util-linux package not installed | Added: 2026-09-12 | Review: 2026-09-26
CVE-2026-53614  # HIGH | util-linux SUID mount(8) nosuid/noexec bypass via LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2 (libuuid 2.42.1-r0, fix 2.42.3-r0) | mount(8) is busybox here; util-linux package not installed | Added: 2026-09-12 | Review: 2026-09-26
CVE-2026-76642  # HIGH | util-linux privileged X-mount post-hooks run after a failed mount helper (libuuid 2.42.1-r0, fix 2.42.3-r0) | mount(8) is busybox here; util-linux package not installed | Added: 2026-09-12 | Review: 2026-09-26
CVE-2026-78408  # HIGH | util-linux nsenter --join-cgroup leaks root cgroup migration authority (libuuid 2.42.1-r0, fix 2.42.3-r1) | nsenter(1) is busybox here; util-linux package not installed | Added: 2026-09-12 | Review: 2026-09-26
CVE-2026-78409  # HIGH | util-linux X-mount.subdir escapes via intermediate symlinks (libuuid 2.42.1-r0, fix 2.42.3-r0) | mount(8) is busybox here; util-linux package not installed | Added: 2026-09-12 | Review: 2026-09-26
CVE-2026-78410  # HIGH | util-linux restricted bind mounts do not pin the source (libuuid 2.42.1-r0, fix 2.42.3-r0) | mount(8) is busybox here; util-linux package not installed | Added: 2026-09-12 | Review: 2026-09-26
